libcamera software ISP: GPU debayer statistics over the whole frame

The GPU debayer (DebayerEGL) scales the whole input frame to the output size,
and process() hands the whole input buffer to the statistics. configure()
still set the statistics window to the output size from the origin, so with
1640x1232 in and 640x480 out, exposure and white balance only looked at the
top-left 39 % of the picture (sky and background for the mower). The window
is now the whole input frame.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
index 4d0caa6..2963382 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -341,10 +341,12 @@ int DebayerEGL::configure(const StreamConfiguration &inputCfg,
 	window_.height = outputCfg.size.height;
 
 	/*
-	 * Don't pass x,y from window_ since process() already adjusts for it.
-	 * But crop the window to 2/3 of its width and height for speedup.
+	 * The shader scales the whole input frame to the output size, and
+	 * process() passes the whole input buffer to the statistics: gather
+	 * them over the whole frame. The output-sized window from the origin
+	 * only covered the top-left corner when scaling down.
 	 */
-	stats_->setWindow(Rectangle(window_.size()));
+	stats_->setWindow(Rectangle(inputCfg.size));
 
 	return 0;
 }
